    "notes": "Official Strat-O-Matic correction: the 2014 set's Aroldis Chapman (Cin) basic side was misprinted, and Strat-O-Matic posted this corrected basic card image on its 2014 Baseball Card Corrections announcement (sourceUrl; image at sourceImage, a 3311x5922 scan). Read twice: (1) from a full-card downscale, (2) from full-resolution per-column crops; no differences. The card prints no hit results at all: every hit comes from the X chances (fielding chart) and the batter's card. X chances print without spaces ('GROUND-BALL(ss)X', wrapped as 'GROUND-' / 'BALL(ss)X'; 'FLYBALL' / '(cf)X'); raw keeps that, outcomes need no change (the normalizer reads both). Validator CHECK (kept, genuine card limitation): SO error .143 and hits .032. Chapman struck out 52% of the batters he faced in 2014 (106 of 202 TBF; Lahman agrees with every printed stat), more than a 108-chance pitcher card can express when half of all plate appearances read the batter's card. Strat-O-Matic maxed the card out instead: 60 strikeout chances (column 6 is all strikeouts except one X chance), 18 walk chances, 30 X chances and no printed hits, which against the league-average batter card implies 38.4% strikeouts (actual 52.7%) and .137 hits per PA (actual .104); walks fit exactly (.119)."
  }
